{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"069a6643-7890-4130-9943-8935e6926b2b","step":{"id":"s1","script":"A derivative measures the slope of a curve at one point. Let's use y equals x squared.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"idea","region":"left","content":"Derivative = slope at a point"},{"op":"axes","id":"graph","region":"right","x":{"min":-1,"max":2,"label":"x"},"y":{"min":-1,"max":4,"label":"y"}},{"op":"curve","id":"parabola","axes_id":"graph","expr":"x^2","domain":[-1,2]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.warning","request_id":"069a6643-7890-4130-9943-8935e6926b2b","code":"step_repaired","step_hint":"s2"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"069a6643-7890-4130-9943-8935e6926b2b","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Focus on the point one, one. A nearby point gives a secant line whose slope is rise over run.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"point","anchor":{"el":"idea","side":"below","gap":0.08},"content":"P = (1,1), Q = (1+h,(1+h)^2)"},{"op":"equation","id":"secant","anchor":{"el":"point","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"m_{\\mathrm{sec}}=\\frac{(1+h)^2-1}{h}=2+h\\quad(h\\neq0)"},{"op":"curve","id":"secantline","axes_id":"graph","expr":"2.5*x-1.5","domain":[0.2,2]},{"op":"text","id":"secantlabel","anchor":{"el":"graph","side":"below","gap":0.04},"content":"Secant shown: h = 0.5, slope = 2.5"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"069a6643-7890-4130-9943-8935e6926b2b","step":{"id":"s3","script":"As the nearby point approaches our chosen point, h approaches zero. The secant slope approaches two.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"limit","anchor":{"el":"secant","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"f'(1)=\\lim_{h\\to0}(2+h)=2"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"What happens to the secant slope as h approaches zero?","expected_gist":"It approaches two, the derivative at x equals one."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"069a6643-7890-4130-9943-8935e6926b2b","step":{"id":"s4","script":"The limiting line is the tangent. Its slope is two, so near this point, y changes about twice as fast as x.","ops":[{"op":"curve","id":"tangent","axes_id":"graph","expr":"2*x-1","domain":[0,2]},{"op":"text","id":"tangentlabel","anchor":{"el":"secantlabel","side":"below","gap":0.06},"content":"Tangent: y = 2x - 1"},{"op":"text","id":"conclusion","anchor":{"el":"limit","side":"below","gap":0.08},"content":"At x = 1: tangent slope = f'(1) = 2"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.done","request_id":"069a6643-7890-4130-9943-8935e6926b2b","accepted_steps":4,"repairs":1,"dropped_steps":0,"sanitized_steps":0,"sanitized_fields":0}
